# Odoo OWL Rule

## Version pin
- Detect version first (`${ODOO_VERSION}` or nearest `__manifest__.py`).
- OWL: v14 none (legacy Widget); v15 OWL 1.x; v16-18 OWL 2.x; v19+ OWL 3.x (stricter static props).

## Stable syntax (v16+)
- `/** @odoo-module **/`
- `import { Component, useState } from "@odoo/owl"`
- Services: `import { useService } from "@web/core/utils/hooks"` (not `@odoo/owl`) — confirmed in `web/static/src/core/utils/hooks.js`
- Register assets under `web.assets_backend` (or website bundles) in `__manifest__.py`
- Do not invent hooks (e.g. fictional `useVisible` / `useIntersectionObserver`)

## Verify with MCP-code when needed
- Prefer `codemode_search` → `codemode_execute` for registries, services, and OWL/XML templates.
- Keep components small; sanitize `t-esc`; do not expose secrets in templates.
